  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\), point \\(D\\) lies on the extension of \\(BC\\). Given \\(\\angle ACD=130^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle A=50^\\circ\\), find the measure of \\(\\angle B\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "80",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\angle ACD\\) is an exterior angle of \\(\\triangle ABC\\), so \\(\\angle ACD=\\angle A+\\angle B\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle B=130^\\circ-50^\\circ=80^\\circ\\).",
